{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For I heard them saying.</b> The word אותם is missing: <b>כי שמעתי</b> אותם <b>אומרים</b> — 'for I heard them saying.' <b>Let us go to Dothan.</b> The Rabbis of blessed memory in their Midrash made it from the expression of נכלי דתות (snares of death), for the angel wished to reveal to Joseph their evil intent. But Joseph did not understand what was hidden within the expression, namely נכלי דתות, and he followed the surface meaning and pursued them and found them in Dothan. This is what they said in the Midrash: 'they journeyed from here' — they removed themselves from brotherhood, and 'went to seek for you נכלי דתות' — snares with which to kill you. And this is what is written: ״ויתנכלו אותו להמיתו״ — they schemed against him to put him to death: they were devising stratagems how to bring about his death without needing to kill him themselves with their own hands. And from here the Rabbis of blessed memory derived what they said: 'they set the dogs upon him.' And perhaps this is what they did before he drew near to them, but it did not succeed in their hands; therefore when he drew near to them they said to kill him by hand, and this is what is written: ״הנה בעל החלומות הלזה בא ועתה לכו ונהרגהו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:17.549014057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}